  "bodyTextSample": "Skip to Main Content\nContact Us\nEnglish\nAccount & Billing\nServices & Outages\nSave Energy & Money\nClean Energy\nSearch\nLog in or Register\nHome\nRebates, Incentives & Credits\n\nRecycling\n\nGet Rewarded for Recycling\n \n\nEarn $50 for each old working appliance you recycle at one of our drop-off events.\n\nDOWNLOAD PARTICIPATION FORM\nAbout Upcoming Events Get Started FAQs\nAbout\nResidential Rockland Electric customers can earn $50* for recycling old, working appliances at designated drop-off locations. Appliances will be recycled responsibly, and customers can put their rebate toward a new, more energy-efficient appliance.\n\nCustomers can drop off up to four room air conditioners and dehumidifiers per event, with a maximum of 12 units through June 20, 2027. In order to receive a rebate, qualifying appliances must:\n\n\nBe a dehumidifier or room air conditioner manufactured no later than 2019\nBe in working condition, with no exposed wiring or sharp edges, to ensure safe handling\nBACK TO TOP \nUpcoming Events\n\nUpcoming Date(s)\n\n\t\n\nLocation\n\n\t\n\nTime\n\n\n\n\nSunday, Sep 20, 2026\n\n\t\n\nThe Home Depot, 465 Route 17, Mahwah, NJ\n\n\t\n\n9:00 A.M.–12:00 P.M.\n\n\n\n\nSunday, Oct 18, 2026\n\n\t\n\nThe Home Depot, 465 Route 17, Mahwah, NJ\n\n\t\n\n9:00 A.M.–12:00 P.M.\n\nBACK TO TOP \nGet Started\nStep 1: Ensure Eligibility\nRockland Electric residential customers aged 18 or older can bring up to four eligible appliances per event (maximum 12 appliances) through June 20, 2027. Review the program’s terms and conditions to confirm your appliance is eligible.\nStep 2: Bring Your Appliance and Participation Form\nFind an upcoming event and bring your eligible appliance and a completed participation form.\nStep 3: Receive Your Reward\nFor every eligible appliance you drop off, you will receive a $50 check by mail sent to your account address approximately six weeks after the event. For more information on receiving your reward, visit the program’s terms and conditions.\nBACK TO TOP \nFAQs\nEXPAND ALL\nQ: Do I need to own the appliance?\nQ: What condition does my appliance need to be in?\nQ: Why does my appliance need to be in working condition to receive a rebate?\nQ: What happens if my appliance is not eligible?\nQ: I want a new energy-efficient appliance. Where can I purchase one?\nBACK TO TOP \n\nGet Rebates and Incentives\n\nFind rebates and incentives for new energy-efficient appliances.\n\nFIND REBATES\n\nSmart Thermostat Rebate\n\nGet an $85 rebate when you enroll your smart thermostat in the Smart Savers program.\n\nENROLL YOUR THERMOSTAT\n\nMy ORU Store\n\nExplore our online marketplace for new energy-efficient appliances.\n\nSHOP NOW\n* Customers may receive a $50 rebate for each qualifying appliance, subject to program eligibility requirements. A maximum of 12 appliances per customer may be rebated during the program period through June 20, 2027, for a maximum potential rebate of $600, which could trigger tax implications.\nOutages\nReport Outage Status\nView Outage Map\nSafety\nBeware of Scammers\nGas Safety\nElectric Safety\nElectric Vehicle Safety\nCarbon Monoxide Safety\nOur Transmission Pipeline Integrity Management Plan\nAbout Us\nCompany Information\nCareers\nDiversity at Orange & Rockland\nMedia Center\nRegulatory Guidance & Oversight\nSustainability Report\nRetirees\nCommunity Affairs\nCommunity Partnerships\nFor Teachers & Students\nOur Storm Recovery Plan\nRate Credit for NJ Veterans' Organizations\nCommunity Issues\nContact Us\nContact Us\nFrequently Asked Questions\nRenters and Homeowners\nTips for Lowering Your Energy Bill\nRebates, Incentives & Credits\nEnergy Saving Store\nEnergy Saving Landscaping\nRequest and Share Energy Data\nProject Center – Building and Service Upgrades\nSmall & Medium Businesses\nRebates, Incentives & Credits\nShare My Data\nProject Center – Building and Service Upgrades\nPOWERREADY Electric Vehicle Program\nCommercial & Industrial\nProject Center – Building and Service Upgrades\nRebates, Incentives & Credits\nEconomic Development\nRequest and Share Energy Data\nPOWERREADY Electric Vehicle Program\nBusiness Partners\nBecome a Partner as an Energy Supplier\nAccess Customer Data\nVendor Services\nTransmission Planning\nHosting Capacity and System Data\nBusiness Opportunities\nInvestors\nFinancial Statements and Notes\nSEC Filings (CEI)\nFinancial Press Releases\nStock Quotes\nRates & Tariffs\nNew York Rates & Tariffs\nNew Jersey Rates & Tariffs\nMunicipalities\nMunicipal Outage Information\nRoad Opening Permit Electronic System\nMunicipal Street Light Portal\nSocial\nFACEBOOK\nX\nLINKEDIN\nINSTAGRAM\nPrivacy Statement Accessibility Policy Terms of Service HomeNet \n\n© 2016-2025 Orange and Rockland Utilities, Inc. All Rights Reserved.",
